-- title:
--   Encoding one block into the Fermat ring: result
-- statement:
--   Under the same register hypotheses (stack `GU` starts with `blk`, registers hold $2^P$, $|blk|$, $2^{2|blk|P}$, $F$), the program `encP` consumes the block and pushes on `EO` the integer $E$ if $E\ge0$ and $E+F$ otherwise, where $E = \mathrm{encRaw}(P, blk) = \bigl(\kappa(\mathrm{re}^+) - \kappa(\mathrm{re}^-)\bigr) + \bigl(\kappa(\mathrm{im}^+) - \kappa(\mathrm{im}^-)\bigr)2^{2|blk|P}$ with $\kappa = $ `kpack (2^P)` applied to the positive and negative parts of the real and imaginary coordinates.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The machine layer: `IState HS` is a state with $64$ stacks of items (`Item` = integer or mark), an input position and an output; `RM` programs (straight-line register code `RS`, loops `rep`, conditionals, calls of the multiplication procedure through a `MulSpec` $M$ giving its domain and cost) have a functional semantics `p.run s`, a definedness predicate `p.ok M s` and a cost `p.cost M s`; `Spec M p s s' c` abbreviates `p.ok M s ∧ p.run s = s' ∧ p.cost M s ≤ c`. `ints L` / `gints U` push an integer list / a list of pairs as items (head = top); `zsz z` is the bit length of $|z|$. `MulBnd M m Φ` says the multiplication procedure accepts all pairs of integers of bit length $\le m$ at cost $\le Φ$. Register names (`GU`, `CR`, `KB`, `XN`, …) are fixed stack indices.
-- source:
--   D. Harvey, J. van der Hoeven, Integer multiplication in time O(n log n), Ann. of Math. 193 (2021), 563–617 (Theorem 1.1: multitape Turing machine multiplication in O(n log n)). Lemma `NLogN.encP_run` of the Lean development NLogN/HEnc.lean (lines 160–219), written for the prove2.me integer-multiplication campaign.

